  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wiqaya: (IWMI) Mitigation of sand and dust storms generation and impacts in Iraq and the Gulf region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Wiqaya project that aims to use evidence-based, locally grounded, and scalable resilient nature based water solution (RNBWS) pilots to mitigate impacts of sand and dust storms (SDS) in Iraq and the broader Gulf region. The Wiqaya project seeks achieve this by: Piloting and building knowledge about the effectiveness of RNBWS to mitigate SDS generation and enhance livelihoods equitably. Improving capability, planning, and dialogue to support scaling of SDS mitigation efforts that leverage national and regional climate finance. Wiqaya is integrated into PHENOMENAL broader regional initiatives - Al Murunah, Al Murunah+ and Jahez</narrative>
  </description>
